course: dictionary
lesson: 13232
title: Reading the look: the word gaze
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gaze is a long, steady look. When a character gazes at something, the author wants you to picture them looking carefully, not just glancing. «Ravi lay on the grass and gazed at the stars.» Gazed tells you Ravi was looking up for a long time, probably dreaming or amazed.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mia gazed out of the window while she thought about her friend.» Thinking and window are the clues: she was looking far away, lost in her thoughts. The word gaze shows the feeling in the scene, not just the action.
explain: Gaze can also be a noun. «The teacher's gaze fell on the empty desk» means her steady look landed on that desk. Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence: "looked at steadily for a long time" fits, so you know you have it right.
fact: Gaze means to look at something steadily for a long time.
fact: A gaze is a long, steady look, and it can be used as a noun.
fact: Gazing often shows that someone is thinking, amazed or interested.
fact: Phrases with gaze: «gaze at», «gaze out of the window», «stargazing», «avert your gaze» (look away), «hold someone's gaze» (keep looking at them).
fact: Look is a simpler word: you can look for one second, but a gaze lasts longer and feels calmer.
exercise: «Ravi lay on the grass and gazed at the stars for an hour.» What does gazed mean? | Shouted loudly | *Looked at steadily for a long time | Ran quickly | Fell asleep
exercise: «Ben looked down and avoided her gaze.» What does gaze mean here? | A loud noise | A cup of tea | A long walk | *A steady look from her eyes
exercise: «Mia gazes out of the window while she thinks.» Find and copy the word that means looks steadily. | while | thinks | *gazes | window
test: «Sam gazed at the painting in the gallery, amazed by its colours.» Why is Sam gazing at the painting? | Because he is late | Because he is hungry | *Because he is amazed and interested | Because he is cold
test: «Ella held her friend's gaze and smiled.» What does held her friend's gaze mean? | Grabbed her friend's arm | Ran away | Closed her eyes | *Kept looking steadily at her friend
exam: In «The astronomer's gaze never left the telescope all night», which word means a long, steady look? | night | *gaze | never | telescope
